{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1554740-character-help-automaton-bun","id":1554740,"title":"Character help - Automaton Bun","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-28T12:31:10-07:00","id":1554740,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Character help - Automaton Bun","content":"Well, I have this idea for a character with the automaton form, as genotypical and coactive.<br /> <br /> It's reseambles as a rabbit made of porcelain, with space-time &quot;powers&quot; that has been built/reactivated quite recently, so Acclimation at 0. But I do not know how to make it work properly.<br /> <br /> We're against a lvl 5 conspiration, so 12 points to the variations.<br /> <br /> I have thought in:<br /> <br /> - Carapace at magnitude 3 as Scar-Free Variation prob<br /> - Translocation at magnitude 3<br /> - Heal at magnitude 2/3 prob as I don't know how an automaton Heals and so making it more resistant<br /> - Enhanced speed at 3<br /> <br /> But I don't know if there's more optimal options to fit in the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28959-damedrac","user":"Damedrac","date":". 10-28-2025, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28959-damedrac","name":"Damedrac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T18:13:45-07:00","id":1554753,"title":"","content":"I will first point out the usual thing for the Automaton Form, which is that unless you know what the deviant's body is supposed to do normally and can reasonably estimate its Availability as being below 6, you are probably better off using a Form that isn't meant to model someone whose body is mechanically an object. (Automatons heal Structure at the same rate as lethal damage, and Sluggish Metabolism is a common Natural Scar for them to represent needing to have damage repaired manually.) Weirdly, this might be better modeled as an Uplift.<br /> <br /> The second point, then, is that the standard &quot;what was the Progenitor trying to accomplish/what were the circumstances of this character's Divergence?&quot; question will help steer a lot of questions about Variations. I personally wouldn't conceive of a creature made of porcelain as durable enough for the Armor ratings of mid-level Carapace, and I'd be surprised to see a rabbit-based deviant with no dots in Brachiation or Predator's Cunning. Spacetime powers make a decent basis for some amount of Precognition, and depending on whether you opt to change this from an Automaton you may be able to fit a few dots of Anomalous Biology into the build as Natural Variations.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, it's worth noting that any of the Forms that represent a fundamental change in the body or origins of the deviant also allow you to spend Merit dots on Natural Variations beyond the base amount provided by Threat Level and Origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}